#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""p11_needle_engine.py -- E2: the P11 needle engine (streamed, teacher-forced, exact sequence-chunked).

Lane gpu4 (Claude, 2026-10-13). Design of record: distill/DISTILL_DESIGN_2026-10-12.md §4 S0 P11 and §6 (256k plan);
STAGE_D_WAVE1_STATUS §4.4 E2. It EXTENDS composite/tools/run_omni_frozen_review.py `--stream --teacher-forced`
(1.2.0) by import, not by edit: that file is step 1's live S8 runner and is never modified here. Everything the
stock streamed engine does (meta construction + assign-loading of one block at a time, fp32 RoPE inv_freq, the
head assign with the exact streamed-block gap set, the band logit mask, the GPU occupancy rule) is used from it.

WHAT E2 ADDS

  A stock streamed layer at L = 262,144 materialises 262,144 x 16,640 x 2 B = 8.7 GB per FFN half (17.4 GB for the
  fused gate|up), fp32 attention scores [24, L, L], and the tree's KDA/short-conv reference is a per-position Python
  loop (~25 h per 256k read). E2 runs each streamed block over the sequence in row chunks of --chunk tokens with
  the residual updated in place:

    KDA (gdn)   norm1 -> q/k/v projections -> causal depthwise short conv with the 3-tap history CARRIED across
                chunks -> q/k l2-norm (fla form) + query scale -> gated delta rule with the recurrent state CARRIED
                -> head-wise RMSNorm, SiLU gate, out projection; then x += ffn(norm2(x)) on the same rows.
                Recurrence kernels: `tree`  (the tree's own forward_with_state per chunk: exact, slow),
                                    `loop`  (vectorised conv + the tree's per-position delta-rule loop),
                                    `fla`   (vectorised conv + fla chunk_gated_delta_rule with initial/final state),
                                    `fla-naive-recurrent` / `fla-naive-chunk` (fla's own torch references with the
                                            same arguments as `fla`: the CPU check of E2's fla mapping, 1.1.0).
    gated GQA   pass 1: k/v projections, k RMSNorm, partial RoPE at absolute positions, kept fp32 for all L;
                pass 2 per row chunk: q projection/norm/RoPE, then per query sub-chunk scores = q.k^T / sqrt(D) in
                fp32 against keys [0, end), causal mask on the diagonal block, softmax, @ v; output gate, out proj;
                then x += ffn(norm2(x)). Exact: a query row's softmax over [0, end) equals the tree's softmax over
                [0, L) with the masked tail at finfo.min (exp underflows to exactly 0); only the reduction length
                differs.
    charted     identity on text rows (the tree's ChartedSourceBlock returns exact zeros where it owns no row;
                the parity arm BUILDS each charted block and asserts block(x) == x bitwise).
    embed/head  embed lookup on the CPU (exact anywhere); the final RMSNorm + lm_head run on the CPU for the scored
                rows only (a 262,144 x 317,952 logit tensor is never formed).

PARITY ARM (`parity`, also run by `read --parity-length 4096` before any needle read): the same streamed blocks
run (a) unchunked through the stock layer (`block(x, token_valid_mask=...)`, the stock streamed engine's call) and
(b) chunked through E2, layer-synchronously from the same embedded input. Per layer it records whether the two
residuals are bit-equal and the max abs diff (and, where they differ, the LOCAL diff of E2 run on the reference
input); at the end the scored-position logits are compared (max abs diff, top-1 agreement). `--chunk` defaults
smaller than the parity length so the chunk boundaries are actually crossed.

NEEDLE READ (`build-needles`, `read`): documents of exactly 32,768 / 131,072 / 262,144 tokens (chat template,
thinking off, the review's render_prompt), haystack = held-out eval-split rows (distill/corpus/eval_split) in a
seeded order, one passkey needle (7 random digits, a named archive) at each of 2 depths, the question at the end,
and the answer digits + <|im_end|> teacher-forced. A no-needle control at 32k reads the same question. Read per
document: first-digit argmax hit / rank / logprob, every-digit argmax hit (exact passkey under teacher forcing),
mean NLL over the digits, stop predicted after the digits. Finite numbers are diagnostics (OMNI1 is the baseline
D2/D4 must not fall below, same engine + same needle file); a non-finite logit or a shape/identity failure is
functional (exit 3).

    build-needles --tokenizer-dir T --filler eval_rows.jsonl --out DIR [--lengths 4096,32768,131072,262144]
    parity        --model M --needles DIR --length 4096 --device cpu --dtype float32 --kda-kernel loop --out R.json
    read          --model M --needles DIR --lengths 32768,131072,262144 --device cuda:0 --dtype bfloat16
                  --kda-kernel fla --parity-length 4096 --out-dir $OC/distill/tps --label p11_omni1
    rescore       --needles DIR --receipts R1.json,R2.json,... --out RESCORE.json       (1.0.0 receipts, CPU)
    recurrence-parity --model M --needles DIR --device cpu --layers 0,1,2,4 --lengths 256,4096
                  --chunks 96,1024 --arms loop,fla-naive-recurrent,fla-naive-chunk --out R.json   (fp32)

SCORING (1.1.0).  Each digit position is read three ways: `strict` = argmax over every unmasked row (1.0.0),
`content` = argmax with the tokenizer's added / special tokens removed (an empty answer, `</think>`, `<tool_call>`
cannot win), `digit` = argmax over the ten digit ids.  Per readout: per-position hit, partial hits n/7, exact
passkey, first-digit hit.  `control_mass` is the probability the model puts on control tokens at each digit slot:
the "empty answer" pull that D2's EOS supervision must not make worse.

Exit codes: 0 written, 3 refusal / functional failure (receipt written when one can be), 1 unexpected error.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import hashlib
import importlib.util
import json
import math
import os
import random
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any, Callable, Sequence

TOOL_NAME = "p11_needle_engine"
TOOL_VERSION = "1.1.0"
# 1.1.0 (lane p2p11, 2026-10-14): the OMNI1 baseline of 2026-10-13 read hit=0 exact=0 in all 7 documents.  The
# documents were already in the no-think form (`<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n` + the digits); what
# 1.0.0 scored was the plain argmax over the whole vocabulary, and OMNI1 puts a CONTROL token on top at the answer
# slot (`<|im_end|>` at 32k / 128k = an empty answer, a second `</think>` at 256k) and sometimes mid-key, while every
# non-control argmax it made was the right digit.  1.1.0 scores three readouts per position -- `strict` (1.0.0's),
# `content` (argmax with the tokenizer's added / special tokens excluded: "score past the control token") and
# `digit` (argmax over the ten digit ids) -- with exact and partial hits for each, the control-token probability
# mass per position, and the top-16 of every scored row in the receipt so a later rescoring never needs a rerun.
# `rescore` recovers what 1.0.0 receipts allow (the argmax string + the first row's top-5 and rank), marking the
# rest unknown.  `recurrence-parity` is the fp32 arm the fla path never had: the KDA mixer of real OMNI1 layers on
# a real needle prefix, the tree's own forward_with_state against E2's recurrences -- `loop`, fla's torch
# references `fla-naive-recurrent` / `fla-naive-chunk` (CPU) and the triton `fla` kernel (CUDA) -- unchunked and
# across E2 chunk boundaries, output and final state.
NEEDLE_SCHEMA = "omni-campaign.p11.needles.v1"
RECEIPT_SCHEMA = "omni-campaign.p11.read.v1"
PARITY_SCHEMA = "omni-campaign.p11.e2-parity.v1"
OC = Path(os.environ.get("OC", "/home/cereal/omni-campaign"))
DEFAULT_REVIEW_TOOL = OC / "composite" / "tools" / "run_omni_frozen_review.py"
DEFAULT_TREE = OC / "import" / "rq27b" / "tree_ef1ffb9"
DEFAULT_CALIBRATION = OC / "calibration"
EXIT_REFUSED = 3
KEY_DIGITS = 7
SENTINEL = "⟦P11-DOCUMENT⟧"
ARCHIVES = ("Kestrel", "Marlow", "Juniper", "Halcyon", "Corvid", "Thistle", "Ostrander", "Vellum", "Quarry", "Brightwater",
            "Ironbark", "Saffron", "Lantern", "Moraine", "Pellucid", "Tamarack", "Wren", "Cobalt", "Ember", "Fallow")


class Refusal(RuntimeError):
    def __init__(self, message: str, *, receipt: dict[str, Any] | None = None):
        super().__init__(message)
        self.receipt = receipt


def log(message: str) -> None:
    print(f"[{time.strftime('%H:%M:%S')}] {message}", flush=True)


def file_sha256(path: str | Path) -> str:
    digest = hashlib.sha256()
    with open(path, "rb") as handle:
        for block in iter(lambda: handle.read(1 << 22), b""):
            digest.update(block)
    return digest.hexdigest()


def ids_sha256(ids: Sequence[int]) -> str:
    return hashlib.sha256(b"".join(int(i).to_bytes(4, "little", signed=True) for i in ids)).hexdigest()


def write_json(path: str | Path, obj: Any) -> str:
    path = Path(path)
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = path.with_name(path.name + f".tmp{os.getpid()}")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(obj, indent=1, sort_keys=True, default=str) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    os.replace(tmp, path)
    return file_sha256(path)


def rss_gb() -> dict[str, float | None]:
    out: dict[str, float | None] = {"rss_gb": None, "peak_rss_gb": None}
    try:
        for line in Path("/proc/self/status").read_text().splitlines():
            if line.startswith("VmRSS:"):
                out["rss_gb"] = round(int(line.split()[1]) / 1e6, 3)
            elif line.startswith("VmHWM:"):
                out["peak_rss_gb"] = round(int(line.split()[1]) / 1e6, 3)
    except OSError:
        pass
    return out


def chunks(length: int, size: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:
    if size < 1:
        raise Refusal(f"chunk size must be >= 1, got {size}")
    return [(s, min(length, s + size)) for s in range(0, length, size)]


# ======================================================================================
# binding the stock streamed engine (read-only import of step 1's runner)
# ======================================================================================


def load_review_tool(path: str | Path) -> Any:
    path = Path(path)
    if not path.is_file():
        raise Refusal(f"no review runner at {path}")
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("run_omni_frozen_review_for_p11", path)
    if spec is None or spec.loader is None:
        raise Refusal(f"cannot import {path}")
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    sys.modules["run_omni_frozen_review_for_p11"] = module
    spec.loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


# ======================================================================================
# needle documents (pure apart from the tokenizer)
# ======================================================================================


def needle_sentence(archive: str, key: str) -> str:
    return f"The secret passkey for the {archive} archive is {key}. Remember this passkey."


def question_text(archive: str) -> str:
    return f"What is the secret passkey for the {archive} archive? Answer with the passkey digits only."


def filler_rows(path: str | Path, *, seed: int) -> list[str]:
    """Held-out eval-split rows as haystack text, in a seeded order (instruction + response per row)."""

    rows: list[str] = []
    with open(path, "r", encoding="utf-8") as handle:
        for line in handle:
            if not line.strip():
                continue
            row = json.loads(line)
            text = "\n".join(str(row.get(k, "")).strip() for k in ("instruction", "response") if str(row.get(k, "")).strip())
            if text:
                rows.append(text)
    if not rows:
        raise Refusal(f"{path}: no filler rows")
    random.Random(int(seed)).shuffle(rows)
    return rows


def tokenize_filler(encode: Callable[[str], list[int]], rows: Sequence[str], need: int) -> tuple[list[int], list[int], int]:
    """Concatenated filler ids (each row + a blank line) and the row-boundary offsets; rows cycle if short."""

    ids: list[int] = []
    bounds: list[int] = [0]
    cycles = 0
    while len(ids) < need:
        for text in rows:
            ids.extend(encode(text + "\n\n"))
            bounds.append(len(ids))
            if len(ids) >= need:
                break
        else:
            cycles += 1
            continue
        break
    return ids, bounds, cycles


def assemble(*, length: int, prefix: list[int], suffix: list[int], question: list[int], needle: list[int] | None,
             answer: list[int], stop: int, filler: list[int], bounds: list[int], depth: float) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """One document of EXACTLY `length` ids: prefix + filler[:i] + needle + filler[i:F] + question + suffix + answer + stop."""

    fixed = len(prefix) + len(suffix) + len(question) + len(answer) + 1 + (len(needle) if needle else 0)
    budget = int(length) - fixed
    if budget <= 0:
        raise Refusal(f"length {length} leaves no room for filler ({fixed} fixed ids)")
    if len(filler) < budget:
        raise Refusal(f"filler has {len(filler)} ids, document needs {budget}")
    body = filler[:budget]
    insert = None
    if needle:
        target = depth * budget
        candidates = [b for b in bounds if 0 < b < budget] or [int(round(target))]
        insert = min(candidates, key=lambda b: (abs(b - target), b))
        body = body[:insert] + list(needle) + body[insert:]
    ids = list(prefix) + body + list(question) + list(suffix) + list(answer) + [int(stop)]
    if len(ids) != int(length):
        raise Refusal(f"assembled {len(ids)} ids, wanted {length}")
    prompt_len = len(ids) - len(answer) - 1
    return {
        "ids": ids, "prompt_tokens": prompt_len, "answer_tokens": len(answer), "filler_tokens": budget,
        "needle_start": None if insert is None else len(prefix) + insert,
        "needle_end": None if insert is None else len(prefix) + insert + len(needle),
        "needle_depth_actual": None if insert is None else insert / budget,
        # position t predicts ids[t + 1]: the digits are predicted at prompt_len - 1 ..; the stop right after them
        "scored_positions": list(range(prompt_len - 1, prompt_len + len(answer))),
    }


def build_needles(*, tokenizer: Any, render: Callable[[list[dict[str, Any]]], str], filler_path: str | Path,
                  lengths: Sequence[int], depths: Sequence[float], control_lengths: Sequence[int], seed: int,
                  stop_token: str = "<|im_end|>") -> dict[str, Any]:
    def encode(text: str) -> list[int]:
        return [int(x) for x in tokenizer(text, add_special_tokens=False, return_tensors=None)["input_ids"]]

    stop = tokenizer.convert_tokens_to_ids(stop_token)
    if not isinstance(stop, int) or stop < 0 or stop == getattr(tokenizer, "unk_token_id", None):
        raise Refusal(f"the tokenizer has no {stop_token!r} token")
    rendered = render([{"role": "user", "content": SENTINEL}])
    if rendered.count(SENTINEL) != 1:
        raise Refusal("the chat template did not render the document sentinel exactly once")
    head, tail = rendered.split(SENTINEL)
    prefix, suffix = encode(head), encode(tail)
    rows = filler_rows(filler_path, seed=seed)
    filler, bounds, cycles = tokenize_filler(encode, rows, max(int(n) for n in lengths) + 64)
    rng = random.Random(int(seed) * 1_000_003 + 11)
    docs: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
    archives = list(ARCHIVES)
    rng.shuffle(archives)
    k = 0
    for length in lengths:
        plan = [(d, True) for d in depths] + ([(float(depths[0]), False)] if int(length) in {int(c) for c in control_lengths} else [])
        for depth, with_needle in plan:
            archive = archives[k % len(archives)]
            k += 1
            key = str(rng.randint(1, 9)) + "".join(str(rng.randint(0, 9)) for _ in range(KEY_DIGITS - 1))
            answer = encode(key)
            if len(answer) != KEY_DIGITS:
                raise Refusal(f"the tokenizer splits the {KEY_DIGITS}-digit key into {len(answer)} ids, expected one per digit")
            needle = encode(needle_sentence(archive, key) + "\n\n")
            question = encode("\n\n" + question_text(archive))
            doc = assemble(length=int(length), prefix=prefix, suffix=suffix, question=question,
                           needle=needle if with_needle else None, answer=answer, stop=stop, filler=filler, bounds=bounds,
                           depth=float(depth))
            doc_id = f"L{int(length)}-d{int(round(float(depth) * 100)):02d}" + ("" if with_needle else "-control")
            doc.update({"id": doc_id, "length": int(length), "depth": float(depth), "needle": with_needle,
                        "archive": archive, "key": key, "answer_ids": answer, "stop_id": int(stop),
                        "ids_sha256": ids_sha256(doc["ids"])})
            docs.append(doc)
    return {"docs": docs, "prefix_sha256": ids_sha256(prefix), "suffix_sha256": ids_sha256(suffix),
            "prefix_tokens": len(prefix), "suffix_tokens": len(suffix), "filler_tokens_available": len(filler),
            "filler_rows": len(rows), "filler_cycles": cycles, "template_rendered_sha256": hashlib.sha256(rendered.encode()).hexdigest()}


def save_needles(out: Path, built: dict[str, Any], meta: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    import torch
    from safetensors.torch import save_file

    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tensors = {d["id"]: torch.tensor(d["ids"], dtype=torch.int32) for d in built["docs"]}
    save_file(tensors, str(out / "needles.safetensors"))
    manifest = {"schema": NEEDLE_SCHEMA, "tool": TOOL_NAME, "tool_version": TOOL_VERSION, "tool_sha256": file_sha256(__file__),
                **meta, **{k: v for k, v in built.items() if k != "docs"},
                "needles_sha256": file_sha256(out / "needles.safetensors"),
                "docs": [{k: v for k, v in d.items() if k != "ids"} for d in built["docs"]]}
    write_json(out / "manifest.json", manifest)
    return manifest


def load_needles(directory: str | Path) -> tuple[dict[str, Any], dict[str, list[int]]]:
    from safetensors.torch import load_file

    directory = Path(directory)
    manifest = json.loads((directory / "manifest.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    if manifest.get("schema") != NEEDLE_SCHEMA:
        raise Refusal(f"{directory}: not a {NEEDLE_SCHEMA} needle set")
    if file_sha256(directory / "needles.safetensors") != manifest["needles_sha256"]:
        raise Refusal(f"{directory}/needles.safetensors does not match its manifest")
    tensors = load_file(str(directory / "needles.safetensors"))
    ids = {d["id"]: [int(x) for x in tensors[d["id"]].tolist()] for d in manifest["docs"]}
    for d in manifest["docs"]:
        if ids_sha256(ids[d["id"]]) != d["ids_sha256"] or len(ids[d["id"]]) != d["length"]:
            raise Refusal(f"needle document {d['id']} does not match its recorded sha / length")
    return manifest, ids


# ======================================================================================
# E2 kernels (exact chunked pieces of ChimeraBlock; tested against the stock layer)
# ======================================================================================


def short_conv_vectorized(conv: Any, x: Any, history: Any | None) -> tuple[Any, Any]:
    """CausalDepthwiseShortConv.forward_with_state for an all-valid chunk, without the per-position loop.

    Same arithmetic per output element: (window * weight).sum(-1) in x.dtype, + bias, SiLU; the next history is the
    last kernel-1 inputs (all rows valid)."""

    import torch
    import torch.nn.functional as F

    kernel = int(conv.kernel_size)
    channels = int(conv.conv.in_channels)
    batch, seq, width = x.shape
    if width != channels:
        raise ValueError("short-convolution input must be [batch, sequence, channels]")
    hist_len = kernel - 1
    if history is None:
        hist = x.new_zeros((batch, channels, hist_len))
    else:
        if tuple(history.shape) != (batch, channels, hist_len):
            raise ValueError(f"short-convolution state must have shape {(batch, channels, hist_len)}")
        hist = history.to(device=x.device, dtype=x.dtype)
    full = torch.cat((hist, x.transpose(1, 2)), dim=-1)
    windows = full.unfold(-1, kernel, 1)
    weight = conv.conv.weight[:, 0, :].to(dtype=x.dtype)
    value = (windows * weight.view(1, channels, 1, kernel)).sum(dim=-1)
    if conv.conv.bias is not None:
        value = value + conv.conv.bias.to(dtype=x.dtype).view(1, channels, 1)
    value = F.silu(value)
    next_hist = full[:, :, full.shape[-1] - hist_len:] if hist_len else full[:, :, :0]
    return value.transpose(1, 2), next_hist.contiguous()


#: E2's fla-family recurrences.  All take the SAME tensors (q, k already l2-normalised, scaled and repeated to the
#: value heads; g = log retention; beta = sigmoid write strength; scale 1.0; state [B, H, K, V]); the two naive ones
#: are fla's own torch references and run on the CPU, so E2's argument mapping can be checked in fp32 without triton.
FLA_RECURRENCES = ("fla", "fla-naive-recurrent", "fla-naive-chunk")
KDA_KERNELS = ("tree", "loop") + FLA_RECURRENCES


def fla_recurrence(impl: str, q: Any, k: Any, v: Any, g: Any, beta: Any, initial_state: Any) -> tuple[Any, Any]:
    """o [B, T, H, V], final state [B, H, K, V].  Keyword calls only: fla's naive_recurrent takes (q, k, v, beta, g),
    the chunk forms (q, k, v, g, beta) -- a positional call would swap the gate and the write strength silently."""

    if impl == "fla":
        from fla.ops.gated_delta_rule import chunk_gated_delta_rule

        return chunk_gated_delta_rule(q=q, k=k, v=v, g=g, beta=beta, scale=1.0, initial_state=initial_state,
                                      output_final_state=True, use_qk_l2norm_in_kernel=False)
    if impl == "fla-naive-recurrent":
        from fla.ops.gated_delta_rule.naive import naive_recurrent_gated_delta_rule

        return naive_recurrent_gated_delta_rule(q=q, k=k, v=v, beta=beta, g=g, scale=1.0, initial_state=initial_state,
                                                output_final_state=True)
    if impl == "fla-naive-chunk":
        from fla.ops.gated_delta_rule.naive import naive_chunk_gated_delta_rule

        o, state = naive_chunk_gated_delta_rule(q=q, k=k, v=v, g=g, beta=beta, scale=1.0, initial_state=initial_state,
                                                output_final_state=True)
        return o[:, : q.shape[1]], state  # it pads T up to its chunk size on the time axis
    raise Refusal(f"unknown fla recurrence {impl!r}")


def kda_chunk(mixer: Any, normalized: Any, state: Any | None, *, recurrence: str) -> tuple[Any, Any]:
    """KimiDeltaAttention.forward_with_state for one all-valid chunk, with the conv vectorised and the recurrence
    either the tree's per-position delta rule (`loop`) or fla's chunk_gated_delta_rule (`fla`, gdn decay only)."""

    import torch
    import torch.nn.functional as F
    from chimera_omni.modeling.layers import KDAState

    x = normalized
    batch, seq, _ = x.shape
    q, next_q = short_conv_vectorized(mixer.q_conv, mixer.q_proj(x), None if state is None else state.q_conv)
    k, next_k = short_conv_vectorized(mixer.k_conv, mixer.k_proj(x), None if state is None else state.k_conv)
    v, next_v = short_conv_vectorized(mixer.v_conv, mixer.v_proj(x), None if state is None else state.v_conv)
    q = q.reshape(batch, seq, mixer.num_key_heads, mixer.key_head_dim)
    k = k.reshape(batch, seq, mixer.num_key_heads, mixer.key_head_dim)
    v = v.reshape(batch, seq, mixer.num_heads, mixer.value_head_dim)
    q = mixer._normalize_qk(q)
    k = mixer._normalize_qk(k)
    if mixer.query_scale is not None:
        q = q * mixer.query_scale
    q = q.to(dtype=x.dtype)
    k = k.to(dtype=x.dtype)
    if mixer.key_group > 1:
        q = q.repeat_interleave(mixer.key_group, dim=2)
        k = k.repeat_interleave(mixer.key_group, dim=2)
    beta = torch.sigmoid(mixer.write_strength(x).float())
    state_dtype = torch.float32 if x.dtype in {torch.float16, torch.bfloat16} else x.dtype
    if state is None:
        recurrent = torch.zeros(batch, mixer.num_heads, mixer.key_head_dim, mixer.value_head_dim, dtype=state_dtype, device=x.device)
    else:
        recurrent = state.recurrent.to(device=x.device, dtype=state_dtype)
    if recurrence == "loop":
        retention = mixer._retention(x)
        outputs = []
        for position in range(seq):
            recurrent = mixer.delta_rule_update(
                recurrent, k[:, position].to(dtype=state_dtype), v[:, position].to(dtype=state_dtype),
                retention[:, position].to(dtype=state_dtype), beta[:, position].to(dtype=state_dtype),
            )
            outputs.append(torch.einsum("bhk,bhkv->bhv", q[:, position].to(dtype=state_dtype), recurrent))
        recurrent_output = torch.stack(outputs, dim=1).to(dtype=x.dtype)
    elif recurrence in FLA_RECURRENCES:
        if mixer.decay_kind != "gdn":
            raise Refusal(f"the fla recurrence is wired for the gdn decay only, this mixer has {mixer.decay_kind!r}")
        decay_logits = mixer.decay_down(x).view(batch, seq, mixer.num_heads).float() + mixer.decay_bias.view(1, 1, mixer.num_heads)
        g = -mixer.decay_log_scale.exp().view(1, 1, mixer.num_heads) * F.softplus(decay_logits)  # = log(retention)
        out, recurrent = fla_recurrence(recurrence, q.contiguous(), k.contiguous(), v.contiguous(), g.contiguous(),
                                        beta.contiguous(), recurrent.contiguous())
        recurrent_output = out.to(dtype=x.dtype)
        recurrent = recurrent.to(dtype=state_dtype)
    else:
        raise Refusal(f"unknown KDA recurrence {recurrence!r}")
    recurrent_output = mixer.output_norm(recurrent_output)
    projected_gate = mixer.output_gate(x)
    if mixer.output_gate_kind == "silu":
        gate = F.silu(projected_gate.float()).to(dtype=x.dtype)
    else:
        gate = torch.sigmoid(projected_gate)
    gate = gate.view(batch, seq, mixer.num_heads, mixer.value_head_dim)
    y = (gate * recurrent_output).reshape(batch, seq, mixer.value_width)
    return mixer.out(y), KDAState(recurrent=recurrent, q_conv=next_q, k_conv=next_k, v_conv=next_v)


def query_subchunk(heads: int, keys: int, budget_bytes: int, *, cap: int, floor: int = 16) -> int:
    rows = int(budget_bytes) // max(1, heads * keys * 4)
    rows = max(int(floor), (rows // 16) * 16 if rows >= 16 else rows)
    return max(1, min(int(cap), rows))


class E2Kernels:
    """The chunked forward of one ChimeraBlock over a [1, L, H] residual, updated in place."""

    def __init__(self, *, chunk: int, kda_kernel: str, attn_budget_bytes: int, min_query_rows: int = 16):
        if kda_kernel not in KDA_KERNELS:
            raise Refusal(f"--kda-kernel must be one of {', '.join(KDA_KERNELS)}, got {kda_kernel!r}")
        self.chunk = int(chunk)
        self.kda_kernel = kda_kernel
        self.attn_budget_bytes = int(attn_budget_bytes)
        self.min_query_rows = int(min_query_rows)
        self.stats: dict[str, Any] = {"query_rows_min": None}

    def block(self, block: Any, x: Any) -> Any:
        from chimera_omni.modeling.layers import GatedGQAAttention, KimiDeltaAttention

        if getattr(block, "charted", None) is not None:
            return x  # a charted block owns no text row: ChartedSourceBlock writes exact zeros (parity-checked)
        if x.ndim != 3 or x.shape[0] != 1:
            raise Refusal("E2 runs one sequence at a time ([1, L, H])")
        if isinstance(block.mixer, KimiDeltaAttention):
            self._kda(block, x)
        elif isinstance(block.mixer, GatedGQAAttention):
            self._gqa(block, x)
        else:
            raise Refusal(f"E2 has no chunked path for mixer {type(block.mixer).__name__}")
        return x

    @staticmethod
    def _ffn_rows(block: Any, xc: Any) -> Any:
        return xc + block.ffn(block.norm2(xc))

    def _kda(self, block: Any, x: Any) -> None:
        import torch

        state = None
        for s, e in chunks(int(x.shape[1]), self.chunk):
            xc = x[:, s:e]
            normalized = block.norm1(xc)
            if self.kda_kernel == "tree":
                valid = torch.ones((1, e - s), dtype=torch.bool, device=x.device)
                out, state = block.mixer.forward_with_state(normalized, initial_state=state, token_valid_mask=valid)
            else:
                out, state = kda_chunk(block.mixer, normalized, state, recurrence=self.kda_kernel)
            xc = xc + out
            x[:, s:e] = self._ffn_rows(block, xc)

    def _gqa(self, block: Any, x: Any) -> None:
        import torch

        mixer = block.mixer
        length = int(x.shape[1])
        heads, kv_heads, dim = int(mixer.num_heads), int(mixer.num_kv_heads), int(mixer.head_dim)
        groups = heads // kv_heads
        keys = torch.empty((1, kv_heads, length, dim), dtype=torch.float32, device=x.device)
        values = torch.empty((1, kv_heads, length, dim), dtype=torch.float32, device=x.device)
        for s, e in chunks(length, self.chunk):
            normalized = block.norm1(x[:, s:e])
            positions = torch.arange(s, e, device=x.device, dtype=torch.long).view(1, -1)
            k = mixer.k_proj(normalized).view(1, e - s, kv_heads, dim)
            if mixer.k_norm is not None:
                k = mixer.k_norm(k)
            keys[:, :, s:e] = mixer.apply_rope(k.transpose(1, 2), positions).float()
            values[:, :, s:e] = mixer.v_proj(normalized).view(1, e - s, kv_heads, dim).transpose(1, 2).float()
        scale = math.sqrt(dim)
        fill = torch.finfo(torch.float32).min
        for s, e in chunks(length, self.chunk):
            xc = x[:, s:e]
            normalized = block.norm1(xc)
            positions = torch.arange(s, e, device=x.device, dtype=torch.long).view(1, -1)
            q = mixer.q_proj(normalized).view(1, e - s, heads, dim)
            if mixer.q_norm is not None:
                q = mixer.q_norm(q)
            q = mixer.apply_rope(q.transpose(1, 2), positions)  # [1, H, T, D]
            attended = torch.empty((1, heads, e - s, dim), dtype=torch.float32, device=x.device)
            rows = query_subchunk(heads, e, self.attn_budget_bytes, cap=e - s, floor=self.min_query_rows)
            self.stats["query_rows_min"] = rows if self.stats["query_rows_min"] is None else min(rows, self.stats["query_rows_min"])
            for a, b in chunks(e - s, rows):
                qa, qb = s + a, s + b  # absolute query rows
                n = b - a
                qq = q[:, :, a:b].float().reshape(1, kv_heads, groups * n, dim)  # head h = kv * groups + g
                scores = torch.matmul(qq, keys[:, :, :qb].transpose(-1, -2)) / scale  # [1, KVH, G*n, qb]
                allowed = torch.arange(qb, device=x.device).view(1, -1) <= torch.arange(qa, qb, device=x.device).view(-1, 1)
                scores.view(1, kv_heads, groups, n, qb).masked_fill_(~allowed, fill)
                probs = torch.softmax(scores, dim=-1)
                del scores
                attended[:, :, a:b] = torch.matmul(probs, values[:, :, :qb]).view(1, heads, n, dim)
                del probs
            y = attended.transpose(1, 2).reshape(1, e - s, heads * dim).to(dtype=x.dtype)
            del attended
            if mixer.gate_proj is not None:
                y = y * torch.sigmoid(mixer.gate_proj(normalized))
            xc = xc + mixer.out(y)
            x[:, s:e] = self._ffn_rows(block, xc)
        del keys, values


# ======================================================================================
# the engine: stock streamed loader + E2 kernels
# ======================================================================================


class NeedleEngine:
    def __init__(self, rofr: Any, root: Path, *, device: str, dtype: Any, mask_band: bool, kernels: E2Kernels,
                 verify_tensors: bool = False):
        import torch

        self.torch = torch
        self.rofr = rofr
        self.device = device
        self.dtype = dtype
        self.kernels = kernels
        stock_refusal = rofr.refuse_charted
        # The stock engine refuses charted checkpoints by name because it would push MEDIA rows through blocks it
        # never routes via charted_output. E2 reads text rows only, where a charted block is the identity (the tree
        # returns exact zeros off its owned rows; the parity arm proves it per block), so the refusal is lifted for
        # the construction of THIS process's private copy of the stock engine only.
        rofr.refuse_charted = lambda cfg, *, why="": None
        try:
            self.base = rofr.StreamedChimera(root, device="cpu", dtype=dtype, ledger_band_logit_mask=mask_band,
                                             verify_tensors=verify_tensors)
        finally:
            rofr.refuse_charted = stock_refusal
        self.base.device = device  # blocks stream to the compute device; embed / norm / lm_head stay on the CPU
        self.cfg = self.base.cfg
        self.model = self.base.model
        self.charted = set(rofr.charted_indices(self.cfg))
        self.num_layers = int(self.cfg.num_layers)
        self.layer_seconds: list[float] = []

    def build_block(self, index: int) -> Any:
        if index not in self.charted:
            return self.base._build_block(index)
        torch = self.torch
        from chimera_omni.modeling.layers import ChimeraBlock

        with torch.device("meta"):
            block = ChimeraBlock(self.cfg, index)
        self.base._assign(block, self.base.block_names[index], prefix=f"blocks.{index}.")
        spec = block.charted.spec
        block.charted.routed_type_ids = torch.tensor(sorted(int(t) for t in spec.type_ids), dtype=torch.long, device=self.device)
        leftover = [n for n, t in list(block.named_parameters()) + list(block.named_buffers()) if t.is_meta]
        if leftover:
            raise Refusal(f"charted block {index}: tensors never materialised: {leftover[:3]}")
        block.eval()
        self.base.block_loads += 1
        return block

    def embed(self, ids: Sequence[int]) -> Any:
        torch = self.torch
        t = torch.tensor([list(ids)], dtype=torch.long)
        self.model._validate_token_ids(t)
        return self.model.embed(t).to(self.device)

    def head(self, x: Any, positions: Sequence[int]) -> Any:
        """fp32 logits [len(positions), vocab] on the CPU (final RMSNorm + lm_head on the scored rows only)."""

        torch = self.torch
        rows = x[0, list(positions)].to("cpu")
        hidden = self.model.norm(rows.unsqueeze(0))
        logits = self.model.lm_head(hidden)
        if self.base.mask_band:
            logits = self.model._mask_ledger_band_logits(logits)
        return logits[0].float()

    def _sync(self) -> None:
        if self.torch.cuda.is_available() and str(self.device).startswith("cuda"):
            self.torch.cuda.synchronize()

    def run(self, sequences: list[list[int]], positions: list[list[int]], *, label: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
        """E2 forward over every sequence (one streamed pass: each block is loaded once and run on every sequence)."""

        torch = self.torch
        started = time.monotonic()
        with torch.no_grad():
            residuals = [self.embed(s).to("cpu") if len(sequences) > 1 else self.embed(s) for s in sequences]
            for index in range(self.num_layers):
                t0 = time.monotonic()
                if index in self.charted:
                    self.layer_seconds.append(0.0)
                    continue
                block = self.base._build_block(index)
                for b, x in enumerate(residuals):
                    on_device = x.to(self.device) if x.device.type != torch.device(self.device).type else x
                    self.kernels.block(block, on_device)
                    residuals[b] = on_device.to("cpu") if len(sequences) > 1 else on_device
                del block
                self._sync()
                if torch.cuda.is_available():
                    torch.cuda.empty_cache()
                self.layer_seconds.append(time.monotonic() - t0)
                if index % 8 == 0 or index == self.num_layers - 1:
                    log(f"{label}: layer {index}/{self.num_layers - 1} done, {self.layer_seconds[-1]:.1f} s, "
                        f"{sum(len(s) for s in sequences) / max(1e-9, time.monotonic() - started):.1f} tok/s so far")
            logits = [self.head(x, p) for x, p in zip(residuals, positions)]
        wall = time.monotonic() - started
        return {"logits": logits, "wall_seconds": wall, "tokens": sum(len(s) for s in sequences)}

    def parity(self, sequence: list[int], positions: list[int], *, label: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
        """Stock layer vs E2, layer-synchronously from the same embedded input."""

        torch = self.torch
        started = time.monotonic()
        layers: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
        with torch.no_grad():
            x_ref = self.embed(sequence)
            x_e2 = x_ref.clone()
            valid = torch.ones((1, len(sequence)), dtype=torch.bool, device=self.device)
            for index in range(self.num_layers):
                block = self.build_block(index)
                x_in = x_ref.clone()
                x_ref = block(x_ref, token_valid_mask=valid)  # the stock streamed engine's call
                x_ref = torch.where(valid.unsqueeze(-1), x_ref, torch.zeros_like(x_ref))
                row: dict[str, Any] = {"layer": index, "kind": str(self.cfg.block_kind(index))}
                if index in self.charted:
                    row["charted_identity_bit_equal"] = bool(torch.equal(x_ref, x_in))
                self.kernels.block(block, x_e2)
                row["bit_equal"] = bool(torch.equal(x_e2, x_ref))
                row["max_abs_diff"] = float((x_e2.float() - x_ref.float()).abs().max())
                row["ref_max_abs"] = float(x_ref.float().abs().max())
                row["finite"] = bool(torch.isfinite(x_e2).all()) and bool(torch.isfinite(x_ref).all())
                if not row["bit_equal"] and index not in self.charted:
                    local = self.kernels.block(block, x_in.clone())
                    row["local_max_abs_diff"] = float((local.float() - x_ref.float()).abs().max())
                    row["local_bit_equal"] = bool(torch.equal(local, x_ref))
                layers.append(row)
                del block
                if torch.cuda.is_available():
                    torch.cuda.empty_cache()
                if index % 8 == 0 or index == self.num_layers - 1:
                    log(f"{label} parity layer {index} ({row['kind']}): bit_equal {row['bit_equal']} max|d| {row['max_abs_diff']:.3e}"
                        + (f" local {row.get('local_max_abs_diff'):.3e}" if "local_max_abs_diff" in row else ""))
            ref_logits = self.head(x_ref, positions)
            e2_logits = self.head(x_e2, positions)
        top1_ref = ref_logits.argmax(dim=-1)
        top1_e2 = e2_logits.argmax(dim=-1)
        finite = logits_sane(ref_logits) and logits_sane(e2_logits) and all(r["finite"] for r in layers)
        same_mask = bool(torch.equal(torch.isfinite(ref_logits), torch.isfinite(e2_logits)))
        max_diff, ref_max = logits_diff(e2_logits, ref_logits)
        charted_ok = all(r.get("charted_identity_bit_equal", True) for r in layers)
        return {
            "layers": layers, "positions": list(positions), "tokens": len(sequence),
            "all_layers_bit_equal": all(r["bit_equal"] for r in layers),
            "final_residual_max_abs_diff": float((x_e2.float() - x_ref.float()).abs().max()),
            "final_residual_bit_equal": bool(torch.equal(x_e2, x_ref)),
            "logits_bit_equal": bool(torch.equal(e2_logits, ref_logits)),
            "logits_max_abs_diff": max_diff, "logits_ref_max_abs": ref_max, "logits_same_finite_mask": same_mask,
            "top1_agreement": int((top1_ref == top1_e2).sum()), "top1_compared": int(top1_ref.numel()),
            "charted_identity_bit_equal": charted_ok, "finite": finite,
            "wall_seconds": time.monotonic() - started,
        }


# ======================================================================================
# scoring
# ======================================================================================


def logits_sane(logits: Any) -> bool:
    """No NaN, no +inf, and every row has a finite logit (the ledger band mask writes -inf by design)."""

    import torch

    return (not bool(torch.isnan(logits).any()) and not bool(torch.isposinf(logits).any())
            and bool(torch.isfinite(logits).any(dim=-1).all()))


def logits_diff(a: Any, b: Any) -> tuple[float, float]:
    """max |a - b| over the columns finite in both (masked band columns are -inf in both), and max |b| there."""

    import torch

    both = torch.isfinite(a) & torch.isfinite(b)
    if not bool(both.any()):
        return float("nan"), float("nan")
    return float((a[both] - b[both]).abs().max()), float(b[both].abs().max())


READOUTS = ("strict", "content", "digit")
KEEP_TOP = 16


def control_token_ids(tokenizer: Any) -> list[int]:
    """The tokenizer's added and special tokens (chat markup, think tags, tool tags, EOS): never answer content."""

    ids = set(int(i) for i in (getattr(tokenizer, "all_special_ids", None) or []))
    ids |= set(int(i) for i in tokenizer.get_added_vocab().values())
    return sorted(ids)


def digit_token_ids(tokenizer: Any) -> list[int]:
    out = []
    for d in "0123456789":
        ids = tokenizer(d, add_special_tokens=False)["input_ids"]
        if len(ids) != 1:
            raise Refusal(f"the tokenizer splits the digit {d!r} into {ids}")
        out.append(int(ids[0]))
    return out


def readout(digits_logprob: Any, answer: Sequence[int], *, allowed: Any | None = None, banned: Any | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """Argmax per digit position over `allowed` ids (or every id but `banned`): per-position hits, partial, exact."""

    import torch

    lp = digits_logprob.clone()
    if allowed is not None:
        mask = torch.full_like(lp, float("-inf"))
        mask[:, allowed] = 0.0
        lp = lp + mask
    if banned is not None and len(banned):
        lp[:, banned] = float("-inf")
    pred = lp.argmax(dim=-1)
    target = torch.tensor([int(a) for a in answer])
    hits = [bool(h) for h in (pred == target).tolist()]
    return {"pred_ids": [int(p) for p in pred], "hits": hits, "partial": sum(hits), "exact": all(hits),
            "first_digit_hit": hits[0]}


def score_doc(doc: dict[str, Any], logits: Any, *, tokenizer: Any | None = None, control_ids: Sequence[int] | None = None,
              digit_ids: Sequence[int] | None = None, keep_top: int = KEEP_TOP) -> dict[str, Any]:
    import torch

    answer = [int(a) for a in doc["answer_ids"]]
    n = len(answer)
    if tuple(logits.shape[:1]) != (n + 1,):
        raise Refusal(f"{doc['id']}: {logits.shape[0]} scored rows, expected {n + 1}")
    if not logits_sane(logits):
        raise Refusal(f"{doc['id']}: non-finite logits (NaN / +inf, or a row with no finite logit) at the scored rows")
    if tokenizer is not None:
        control_ids = control_token_ids(tokenizer) if control_ids is None else control_ids
        digit_ids = digit_token_ids(tokenizer) if digit_ids is None else digit_ids
    logprob = torch.log_softmax(logits, dim=-1)  # band columns are -inf under the ledger mask: probability 0
    digits = logprob[:n]
    target = torch.tensor(answer)
    picked = digits[torch.arange(n), target]
    argmax = digits.argmax(dim=-1)
    first_rank = int((digits[0] > digits[0, answer[0]]).sum()) + 1
    stop_argmax = int(logprob[n].argmax())
    top5 = [int(t) for t in torch.topk(digits[0], 5).indices]
    out = {
        "id": doc["id"], "length": doc["length"], "depth": doc["depth"], "needle": doc["needle"],
        "needle_depth_actual": doc.get("needle_depth_actual"), "key": doc["key"],
        "first_digit_hit": bool(int(argmax[0]) == answer[0]), "first_digit_rank": first_rank,
        "first_digit_logprob": float(picked[0]), "digits_argmax_agree": int((argmax == target).sum()), "digits": n,
        "passkey_exact_teacher_forced": bool(torch.equal(argmax, target)),
        "mean_nll_digits": float((-picked).mean()), "stop_after_digits": bool(stop_argmax == int(doc["stop_id"])),
        "stop_logprob": float(logprob[n, int(doc["stop_id"])]), "first_digit_top5_ids": top5,
    }
    readouts = {"strict": readout(digits, answer)}
    if control_ids is not None:
        control = torch.tensor(sorted(int(c) for c in control_ids if 0 <= int(c) < digits.shape[-1]), dtype=torch.long)
        readouts["content"] = readout(digits, answer, banned=control)
        mass = digits[:, control].exp().sum(dim=-1) if control.numel() else torch.zeros(n)
        out["control_mass_per_digit"] = [round(float(m), 6) for m in mass]
        out["control_mass_mean"] = float(mass.mean())
        out["control_argmax_positions"] = [i for i, p in enumerate(argmax.tolist()) if int(p) in set(control.tolist())]
    if digit_ids is not None:
        readouts["digit"] = readout(digits, answer, allowed=torch.tensor([int(d) for d in digit_ids], dtype=torch.long))
        out["digit_rank_first"] = int((digits[0, list(digit_ids)] > digits[0, answer[0]]).sum()) + 1
    out["readouts"] = readouts
    k = min(int(keep_top), logprob.shape[-1])
    top = torch.topk(logprob, k, dim=-1)
    out["rows_top"] = {"k": k, "ids": top.indices.tolist(), "logprob": [[round(float(v), 5) for v in row] for row in top.values]}
    if tokenizer is not None:
        out["argmax_text"] = tokenizer.decode([int(a) for a in argmax])
        out["first_digit_top5"] = [tokenizer.decode([t]) for t in top5]
        for name, r in readouts.items():
            r["pred_text"] = tokenizer.decode(r["pred_ids"])
    return out


def summary_token(row: dict[str, Any]) -> str:
    """One document in the P11 SUMMARY line: 1.0.0's strict hit/exact first, then the 1.1.0 readouts."""

    parts = [f"{row['id']} hit={int(row['first_digit_hit'])} exact={int(row['passkey_exact_teacher_forced'])} nll={row['mean_nll_digits']:.2f}"]
    for name in ("content", "digit"):
        r = (row.get("readouts") or {}).get(name)
        if r is not None:
            parts.append(f"{name}={r['partial']}/{len(r['hits'])}{'(exact)' if r['exact'] else ''}")
    if row.get("control_mass_mean") is not None:
        parts.append(f"ctl={row['control_mass_mean']:.2f}")
    return " ".join(parts)


# ======================================================================================
# CLI
# ======================================================================================


def bind(args: argparse.Namespace) -> tuple[Any, dict[str, Any]]:
    rofr = load_review_tool(args.review_tool)
    tree = rofr.bind_chimera_tree(args.chimera_src, None)
    return rofr, tree


def tokenizer_and_render(rofr: Any, args: argparse.Namespace) -> tuple[Any, Callable, dict[str, Any]]:
    from transformers import AutoTokenizer

    oc_calib, _ = rofr.bind_calibration(args.calibration_dir)
    tok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(str(args.tokenizer_dir), trust_remote_code=False)
    render = lambda messages: oc_calib.render_prompt(tok, messages, thinking="off")  # noqa: E731
    files = {p.name: file_sha256(p) for p in sorted(Path(args.tokenizer_dir).glob("tokenizer*.json"))}
    return tok, render, {"tokenizer_dir": str(args.tokenizer_dir), "tokenizer_files_sha256": files,
                         "render": "oc_calib.render_prompt(thinking='off'), add_generation_prompt=True",
                         "oc_calib_sha256": file_sha256(Path(args.calibration_dir) / "oc_calib.py")}


def cmd_build(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    rofr = load_review_tool(args.review_tool)
    tok, render, tinfo = tokenizer_and_render(rofr, args)
    lengths = [int(v) for v in args.lengths.split(",")]
    depths = [float(v) for v in args.depths.split(",")]
    controls = [int(v) for v in args.control_lengths.split(",") if v.strip()]
    built = build_needles(tokenizer=tok, render=render, filler_path=args.filler, lengths=lengths, depths=depths,
                          control_lengths=controls, seed=int(args.seed))
    meta = {**tinfo, "filler": str(args.filler), "filler_sha256": file_sha256(args.filler), "seed": int(args.seed),
            "lengths": lengths, "depths": depths, "control_lengths": controls, "key_digits": KEY_DIGITS,
            "built_utc": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())}
    manifest = save_needles(Path(args.out), built, meta)
    for d in manifest["docs"]:
        log(f"{d['id']}: {d['length']} ids, needle {d['needle']} at {d.get('needle_depth_actual')}, key {d['key']}, "
            f"prompt {d['prompt_tokens']}, sha {d['ids_sha256'][:16]}")
    log(f"needle set {args.out}: {len(manifest['docs'])} docs, needles.safetensors {manifest['needles_sha256'][:16]}, "
        f"filler {manifest['filler_tokens_available']} ids from {manifest['filler_rows']} rows, cycles {manifest['filler_cycles']}")
    return 0


def engine_from_args(rofr: Any, args: argparse.Namespace) -> tuple[NeedleEngine, dict[str, Any]]:
    import torch

    torch.set_grad_enabled(False)
    dtype = {"float32": torch.float32, "bfloat16": torch.bfloat16, "float16": torch.float16}[args.dtype]
    device = str(args.device)
    if not device.startswith("cuda") and dtype != torch.float32:
        raise Refusal("bf16 on the CPU is ~400x slower than fp32; the CPU arm runs --dtype float32")
    if args.kda_kernel == "fla" and not device.startswith("cuda"):
        raise Refusal("--kda-kernel fla needs a CUDA device (triton)")
    placement: dict[str, Any] = {"device": device, "CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES": os.environ.get("CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES"),
                                 "CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER": os.environ.get("CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER")}
    if device.startswith("cuda"):
        inventory = rofr.cuda_inventory([device])
        rofr.check_gpu_free(inventory)
        placement["inventory_at_start"] = inventory
        torch.cuda.reset_peak_memory_stats()
    kernels = E2Kernels(chunk=int(args.chunk), kda_kernel=args.kda_kernel, attn_budget_bytes=int(args.attn_budget_mib) << 20,
                        min_query_rows=int(args.min_query_rows))
    t0 = time.monotonic()
    engine = NeedleEngine(rofr, Path(args.model), device=device, dtype=dtype, mask_band=not args.no_band_mask, kernels=kernels)
    placement["head_load_seconds"] = round(time.monotonic() - t0, 2)
    return engine, placement


def identity_block(args: argparse.Namespace, tree: dict[str, Any], engine: NeedleEngine) -> dict[str, Any]:
    model = Path(args.model)
    index = json.loads((model / "model.safetensors.index.json").read_text()) if (model / "model.safetensors.index.json").is_file() else {}
    manifest = model / "composite_manifest.json"
    return {"model": str(model), "total_size": index.get("metadata", {}).get("total_size"),
            "composite_manifest_sha256": file_sha256(manifest) if manifest.is_file() else None,
            "config_sha256": file_sha256(model / "config.json") if (model / "config.json").is_file() else None,
            "num_layers": engine.num_layers, "charted_blocks": sorted(engine.charted), "chimera_tree": tree,
            "review_tool": str(args.review_tool), "review_tool_sha256": file_sha256(args.review_tool),
            "tool": TOOL_NAME, "tool_version": TOOL_VERSION, "tool_sha256": file_sha256(__file__)}


def memory_block(device: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
    import torch

    out: dict[str, Any] = dict(rss_gb())
    if torch.cuda.is_available() and device.startswith("cuda"):
        out["cuda_max_allocated_mib"] = int(torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated()) >> 20
        out["cuda_max_reserved_mib"] = int(torch.cuda.max_memory_reserved()) >> 20
    return out


def parity_gate(result: dict[str, Any], *, device: str, min_top1: float, max_rel: float) -> dict[str, Any]:
    rel = result["logits_max_abs_diff"] / max(1e-12, result["logits_ref_max_abs"])
    agree = result["top1_agreement"] / max(1, result["top1_compared"])
    structural = result["finite"] and result["charted_identity_bit_equal"] and result["logits_same_finite_mask"]
    if result["logits_bit_equal"]:
        verdict, why = "PASS", "bit-equal"
    elif structural and agree >= min_top1 and (device.startswith("cuda") or rel <= max_rel):
        verdict, why = "PASS", f"max abs diff {result['logits_max_abs_diff']:.3e} (rel {rel:.2e}), top-1 {agree:.4f}"
    else:
        verdict, why = "FAIL", (f"finite {result['finite']} charted identity {result['charted_identity_bit_equal']} "
                                f"top-1 {agree:.4f} (min {min_top1}) rel {rel:.2e} (max {max_rel} on cpu)")
    return {"verdict": verdict, "why": why, "logits_rel_max_abs_diff": rel, "top1_rate": agree,
            "rules": {"min_top1": min_top1, "max_rel_cpu": max_rel, "structural": "finite + every charted block bit-identity"}}


def run_parity_arm(engine: NeedleEngine, manifest: dict[str, Any], ids: dict[str, list[int]], *, length: int,
                   args: argparse.Namespace, base: dict[str, Any], out: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:
    docs = [d for d in manifest["docs"] if d["length"] == int(length) and d["needle"]]
    if not docs:
        raise Refusal(f"the needle set has no {length}-token document for the parity arm")
    doc = docs[0]
    seq = ids[doc["id"]]
    stride = max(1, len(seq) // 64)
    positions = sorted(set(range(0, len(seq), stride)) | set(doc["scored_positions"]))
    log(f"parity arm: {doc['id']} ({len(seq)} tokens), chunk {args.chunk}, kda {args.kda_kernel}, {len(positions)} compared rows")
    result = engine.parity(seq, positions, label=f"{args.label}-parity")
    gate = parity_gate(result, device=str(args.device), min_top1=float(args.parity_min_top1), max_rel=float(args.parity_max_rel))
    receipt = {"schema": PARITY_SCHEMA, **base, "doc": doc["id"], "chunk": int(args.chunk), "kda_kernel": args.kda_kernel,
               "dtype": args.dtype, "attn_budget_mib": int(args.attn_budget_mib), "query_rows_min": engine.kernels.stats["query_rows_min"],
               "result": result, "gate": gate, "memory": memory_block(str(args.device)),
               "written_utc": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())}
    sha = write_json(out, receipt)
    unequal = [r["layer"] for r in result["layers"] if not r["bit_equal"]]
    print(f"E2 PARITY {gate['verdict']} ({args.device}, {args.dtype}, kda {args.kda_kernel}, chunk {args.chunk}, L={len(seq)}): "
          f"layers bit-equal {len(result['layers']) - len(unequal)}/{len(result['layers'])}, final residual max|d| "
          f"{result['final_residual_max_abs_diff']:.3e}, logits max|d| {result['logits_max_abs_diff']:.3e} "
          f"(rel {gate['logits_rel_max_abs_diff']:.2e}), top-1 {result['top1_agreement']}/{result['top1_compared']}, "
          f"charted identity {result['charted_identity_bit_equal']}; {gate['why']}; receipt {out} sha256 {sha[:16]}", flush=True)
    return receipt


def cmd_parity(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    rofr, tree = bind(args)
    manifest, ids = load_needles(args.needles)
    engine, placement = engine_from_args(rofr, args)
    base = {"identity": identity_block(args, tree, engine), "placement": placement, "needles": str(args.needles),
            "needles_sha256": manifest["needles_sha256"], "argv": sys.argv}
    receipt = run_parity_arm(engine, manifest, ids, length=int(args.length), args=args, base=base, out=Path(args.out))
    return 0 if receipt["gate"]["verdict"] == "PASS" else EXIT_REFUSED


def cmd_read(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    rofr, tree = bind(args)
    manifest, ids = load_needles(args.needles)
    from transformers import AutoTokenizer

    tok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(str(manifest["tokenizer_dir"]), trust_remote_code=False)
    control_ids, digit_ids = control_token_ids(tok), digit_token_ids(tok)
    engine, placement = engine_from_args(rofr, args)
    base = {"identity": identity_block(args, tree, engine), "placement": placement, "needles": str(args.needles),
            "needles_sha256": manifest["needles_sha256"], "argv": sys.argv}
    out_dir = Path(args.out_dir)
    status = 0
    if int(args.parity_length) > 0:
        parity = run_parity_arm(engine, manifest, ids, length=int(args.parity_length), args=args, base=base,
                                out=out_dir / f"{args.label}_e2_parity_{args.dtype}_{args.kda_kernel}_L{args.parity_length}.json")
        if parity["gate"]["verdict"] != "PASS":
            raise Refusal(f"E2 parity arm FAILED ({parity['gate']['why']}); no needle read is made on an engine that "
                          "does not reproduce the stock layer")
    summary: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
    for length in [int(v) for v in args.lengths.split(",")]:
        docs = [d for d in manifest["docs"] if d["length"] == length]
        if not docs:
            raise Refusal(f"the needle set has no {length}-token documents")
        if engine.torch.cuda.is_available():
            engine.torch.cuda.reset_peak_memory_stats()
        engine.layer_seconds = []
        label = f"{args.label}-L{length}"
        log(f"{label}: {len(docs)} docs {[d['id'] for d in docs]}")
        try:
            result = engine.run([ids[d["id"]] for d in docs], [d["scored_positions"] for d in docs], label=label)
        except engine.torch.OutOfMemoryError as exc:
            receipt = {"schema": RECEIPT_SCHEMA, **base, "length": length, "refused": "out-of-memory", "error": str(exc)[:2000],
                       "chunk": int(args.chunk), "attn_budget_mib": int(args.attn_budget_mib), "memory": memory_block(str(args.device))}
            write_json(out_dir / f"{args.label}_L{length}.refused.json", receipt)
            log(f"{label}: OUT OF MEMORY, receipt written; stopping (longer lengths would not fit either)")
            status = EXIT_REFUSED
            break
        scored = [score_doc(d, lg, tokenizer=tok, control_ids=control_ids, digit_ids=digit_ids) for d, lg in zip(docs, result["logits"])]
        rate = result["tokens"] / max(1e-9, result["wall_seconds"])
        receipt = {"schema": RECEIPT_SCHEMA, **base, "length": length, "docs": scored,
                   "rate": {"tokens": result["tokens"], "wall_seconds": round(result["wall_seconds"], 2), "tokens_per_second": round(rate, 2),
                            "layer_seconds": [round(s, 2) for s in engine.layer_seconds]},
                   "chunk": int(args.chunk), "kda_kernel": args.kda_kernel, "dtype": args.dtype,
                   "attn_budget_mib": int(args.attn_budget_mib), "query_rows_min": engine.kernels.stats["query_rows_min"],
                   "memory": memory_block(str(args.device)), "band_logit_mask": not args.no_band_mask,
                   "scoring": {"readouts": list(READOUTS), "control_ids": control_ids, "digit_ids": digit_ids, "keep_top": KEEP_TOP},
                   "note": "teacher-forced read: diagnostics, not a grade; OMNI1 is the baseline D2/D4 must not fall below "
                           "(same engine version, same needle file)",
                   "written_utc": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())}
        sha = write_json(out_dir / f"{args.label}_L{length}.json", receipt)
        for s in scored:
            log(f"{label} {s['id']}: first-digit hit {s['first_digit_hit']} rank {s['first_digit_rank']} "
                f"logprob {s['first_digit_logprob']:.3f}; digits {s['digits_argmax_agree']}/{s['digits']} "
                f"exact {s['passkey_exact_teacher_forced']} nll {s['mean_nll_digits']:.3f} stop {s['stop_after_digits']} "
                f"argmax {s.get('argmax_text')!r} key {s['key']}; content {s['readouts']['content']['partial']}/{s['digits']} "
                f"exact {s['readouts']['content']['exact']} {s['readouts']['content'].get('pred_text')!r}; digit "
                f"{s['readouts']['digit']['partial']}/{s['digits']} exact {s['readouts']['digit']['exact']}; control mass "
                f"{s['control_mass_mean']:.3f} at {s['control_argmax_positions']}")
        log(f"{label}: {result['tokens']} tokens in {result['wall_seconds']:.1f} s = {rate:.2f} tok/s; memory {receipt['memory']}; "
            f"receipt sha256 {sha[:16]}")
        summary.extend({"length": length, **{k: s[k] for k in ("id", "needle", "first_digit_hit", "passkey_exact_teacher_forced",
                                                              "mean_nll_digits", "first_digit_rank", "control_mass_mean")},
                        "readouts": {name: {k: r[k] for k in ("partial", "exact", "first_digit_hit", "hits")} for name, r in s["readouts"].items()},
                        "tok_s": round(rate, 2)}
                       for s in scored)
    sha = write_json(out_dir / f"{args.label}_summary.json", {"schema": RECEIPT_SCHEMA + "/summary", **base, "rows": summary,
                                                              "exit": status, "written_utc": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())})
    print("P11 SUMMARY " + "; ".join(summary_token(r) for r in summary) + f" (summary sha256 {sha[:16]})", flush=True)
    return status


# ======================================================================================
# 1.1.0: rescoring 1.0.0 receipts, and the fp32 recurrence parity arm
# ======================================================================================


def rescore_doc(entry: dict[str, Any], answer: Sequence[int], *, encode: Callable[[str], list[int]], control: set[int],
                digits: set[int]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """What a 1.0.0 receipt row still tells about the 1.1.0 readouts.

    1.0.0 kept the strict argmax string of the 7 digit rows plus the first row's top-5 ids and the answer's rank.
    A strict argmax that is not a control token IS the content argmax (and, if a digit, the digit argmax); one
    that is a control token leaves the other readouts unknown -- except on the first row, where the top-5 and the
    rank decide them when the answer (or the first non-control / first digit token) is inside what was kept.
    Every position is True / False / None (unknown); nothing is guessed.
    """

    n = len(answer)
    pred = encode(entry.get("argmax_text") or "")
    out: dict[str, Any] = {"id": entry["id"], "key": entry.get("key"), "needle": entry.get("needle"), "length": entry.get("length")}
    if len(pred) != n:
        out["error"] = f"argmax_text re-encodes to {len(pred)} ids, expected {n}"
        return out
    top5 = [int(t) for t in entry.get("first_digit_top5_ids") or []]
    rank = entry.get("first_digit_rank")
    readouts: dict[str, list[bool | None]] = {"strict": [], "content": [], "digit": []}
    for i, (p, a) in enumerate(zip(pred, answer)):
        readouts["strict"].append(p == a)
        content = digit = None
        if p not in control:
            content = p == a
        if p in digits:
            digit = p == a
        if i == 0 and top5:
            if content is None:
                first = next((t for t in top5 if t not in control), None)
                if first is not None:
                    content = first == a
                elif rank is not None and int(rank) <= len(top5) + 1:
                    content = True  # every token above the answer is a kept control token
            if digit is None:
                first = next((t for t in top5 if t in digits), None)
                if first is not None:
                    digit = first == a
                elif rank is not None and int(rank) <= len(top5) + 1:
                    digit = True  # nothing above the answer is a digit
        readouts["content"].append(content)
        readouts["digit"].append(digit)
    out["readouts"] = {}
    for name, hits in readouts.items():
        known_hit = sum(1 for h in hits if h is True)
        known_miss = sum(1 for h in hits if h is False)
        unknown = sum(1 for h in hits if h is None)
        out["readouts"][name] = {"hits": hits, "known_hits": known_hit, "known_misses": known_miss, "unknown": unknown,
                                 "partial_range": [known_hit, known_hit + unknown],
                                 "exact": False if known_miss else (True if unknown == 0 else None)}
    out["control_argmax_positions"] = [i for i, p in enumerate(pred) if p in control]
    out["wrong_digit_positions"] = [i for i, (p, a) in enumerate(zip(pred, answer)) if p in digits and p != a]
    return out


def cmd_rescore(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    from transformers import AutoTokenizer

    manifest, _ = load_needles(args.needles)
    tok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(str(manifest["tokenizer_dir"]), trust_remote_code=False)
    control, digits = set(control_token_ids(tok)), set(digit_token_ids(tok))
    answers = {d["id"]: [int(a) for a in d["answer_ids"]] for d in manifest["docs"]}

    def encode(text: str) -> list[int]:
        return [int(x) for x in tok(text, add_special_tokens=False)["input_ids"]]

    rows, sources = [], []
    for path in [p for p in args.receipts.split(",") if p.strip()]:
        receipt = json.loads(Path(path).read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        if receipt.get("needles_sha256") != manifest["needles_sha256"]:
            raise Refusal(f"{path} was read on needle set {receipt.get('needles_sha256')}, not {manifest['needles_sha256']}")
        sources.append({"path": str(path), "sha256": file_sha256(path), "tool_version": (receipt.get("identity") or {}).get("tool_version")})
        for entry in receipt.get("docs", []):
            rows.append(rescore_doc(entry, answers[entry["id"]], encode=encode, control=control, digits=digits))
    out = {"schema": RECEIPT_SCHEMA + "/rescore", "tool": TOOL_NAME, "tool_version": TOOL_VERSION, "tool_sha256": file_sha256(__file__),
           "needles": str(args.needles), "needles_sha256": manifest["needles_sha256"], "sources": sources,
           "control_ids": sorted(control), "digit_ids": sorted(digits), "docs": rows,
           "note": "rescored from 1.0.0 receipt fields only (argmax string, first-row top-5 and rank); None = not recoverable "
                   "without a rerun; the 1.1.0 read saves the top-16 of every scored row",
           "written_utc": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())}
    sha = write_json(args.out, out)
    for r in rows:
        if "error" in r:
            log(f"{r['id']}: {r['error']}")
            continue
        parts = [f"{name} {v['known_hits']}/{len(v['hits'])}" + (f" (+{v['unknown']} unknown)" if v["unknown"] else "")
                 + f" exact={v['exact']}" for name, v in r["readouts"].items()]
        log(f"{r['id']} key {r['key']}: " + "; ".join(parts) + f"; control argmax at {r['control_argmax_positions']}, "
            f"wrong digits at {r['wrong_digit_positions']}")
    print("P11 RESCORE " + "; ".join(
        f"{r['id']} strict={r['readouts']['strict']['known_hits']}/7 content={r['readouts']['content']['partial_range'][0]}"
        f"-{r['readouts']['content']['partial_range'][1]}/7 digit={r['readouts']['digit']['partial_range'][0]}"
        f"-{r['readouts']['digit']['partial_range'][1]}/7 wrong_digits={len(r['wrong_digit_positions'])}"
        for r in rows if "error" not in r) + f" (receipt {args.out} sha256 {sha[:16]})", flush=True)
    return 0


def tensor_gap(a: Any, b: Any) -> dict[str, float]:
    a64, b64 = a.double(), b.double()
    ref = float(b64.abs().max())
    gap = float((a64 - b64).abs().max())
    return {"max_abs": gap, "ref_max_abs": ref, "rel": gap / max(ref, 1e-30)}


def cmd_recurrence_parity(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    """fp32 KDA recurrence parity on real OMNI1 layers: the tree's forward_with_state vs E2's recurrences."""

    import torch

    rofr, tree = bind(args)
    manifest, ids = load_needles(args.needles)
    from chimera_omni.modeling.layers import KimiDeltaAttention

    torch.set_grad_enabled(False)
    dtype = {"float32": torch.float32, "float64": torch.float64}[args.dtype]
    device = str(args.device)
    lengths = [int(v) for v in args.lengths.split(",")]
    chunk_sizes = [int(v) for v in args.chunks.split(",")]
    if len(chunk_sizes) != len(lengths):
        raise Refusal("--chunks needs one E2 chunk size per --lengths entry")
    arms = [a.strip() for a in args.arms.split(",") if a.strip()]
    for arm in arms:
        if arm not in KDA_KERNELS or arm == "tree":
            raise Refusal(f"arm {arm!r} is not an E2 recurrence ({', '.join(k for k in KDA_KERNELS if k != 'tree')})")
        if arm == "fla" and not device.startswith("cuda"):
            raise Refusal("the triton fla arm needs a CUDA device; the CPU arms are loop, fla-naive-recurrent, fla-naive-chunk")
    docs = [d for d in manifest["docs"] if d["needle"] and d["length"] >= max(lengths)]
    if not docs:
        raise Refusal(f"no needle document of >= {max(lengths)} tokens")
    doc = min(docs, key=lambda d: d["length"])
    sequence = ids[doc["id"]][: max(lengths)]
    kernels = E2Kernels(chunk=max(chunk_sizes), kda_kernel="loop", attn_budget_bytes=256 << 20)
    engine = NeedleEngine(rofr, Path(args.model), device=device, dtype=dtype, mask_band=True, kernels=kernels)
    kda_layers = [i for i in range(engine.num_layers) if i not in engine.charted and str(engine.cfg.block_kind(i)) == "kda"]
    if args.layers == "auto":
        middle = min(kda_layers, key=lambda i: (abs(i - engine.num_layers // 2), i))
        chosen = sorted(set(kda_layers[:3] + [middle]))
    else:
        chosen = sorted(int(v) for v in args.layers.split(","))
        bad = [i for i in chosen if i not in kda_layers]
        if bad:
            raise Refusal(f"layers {bad} are not KDA blocks (KDA: {kda_layers[:8]}...)")
    log(f"recurrence parity: {doc['id']} prefix {len(sequence)} tokens, layers {chosen}, lengths {lengths} (E2 chunks {chunk_sizes}), "
        f"arms {arms}, {args.dtype} on {device}")
    rows: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
    started = time.monotonic()
    x = engine.embed(sequence).to(dtype)
    valid = torch.ones((1, x.shape[1]), dtype=torch.bool, device=x.device)
    for index in range(max(chosen) + 1):
        block = engine.build_block(index)
        if index in chosen:
            if not isinstance(block.mixer, KimiDeltaAttention):
                raise Refusal(f"layer {index} is not a KDA block")
            normalized_full = block.norm1(x)
            for length, chunk in zip(lengths, chunk_sizes):
                normalized = normalized_full[:, :length].contiguous()
                ref_out, ref_state = block.mixer.forward_with_state(normalized, initial_state=None, token_valid_mask=valid[:, :length])
                for arm in arms:
                    for chunked in (False, True):
                        t0 = time.monotonic()
                        if not chunked:
                            out, state = kda_chunk(block.mixer, normalized, None, recurrence=arm)
                        else:
                            pieces, state = [], None
                            for s, e in chunks(length, chunk):
                                piece, state = kda_chunk(block.mixer, normalized[:, s:e], state, recurrence=arm)
                                pieces.append(piece)
                            out = torch.cat(pieces, dim=1)
                        row = {"layer": index, "length": length, "arm": arm, "chunk": chunk if chunked else None,
                               "boundaries_crossed": (len(chunks(length, chunk)) - 1) if chunked else 0,
                               "output": tensor_gap(out, ref_out), "state": tensor_gap(state.recurrent, ref_state.recurrent),
                               "finite": bool(torch.isfinite(out).all()) and bool(torch.isfinite(state.recurrent).all()),
                               "seconds": round(time.monotonic() - t0, 2)}
                        rows.append(row)
                        log(f"layer {index} L={length} {arm:20s} {'chunk ' + str(chunk) if chunked else 'whole   '}: output rel "
                            f"{row['output']['rel']:.3e} (max|d| {row['output']['max_abs']:.3e} of {row['output']['ref_max_abs']:.3e}), "
                            f"state rel {row['state']['rel']:.3e}, {row['seconds']} s")
        x = block(x, token_valid_mask=valid)
        x = torch.where(valid.unsqueeze(-1), x, torch.zeros_like(x))
        del block
    #: the torch references (loop, fla-naive-*) are exact fp32 algebra: --threshold-rel.  The triton kernel may run its
    #: fp32 dots as TF32 (triton's default on Ampere unless TRITON_F32_DEFAULT=ieee): its own --threshold-rel-kernel
    def bound(arm: str) -> float:
        return float(args.threshold_rel_kernel) if arm == "fla" else float(args.threshold_rel)

    for r in rows:
        r["bound"] = bound(r["arm"])
        r["pass"] = r["finite"] and max(r["output"]["rel"], r["state"]["rel"]) <= r["bound"]
    worst = max(rows, key=lambda r: max(r["output"]["rel"], r["state"]["rel"]) / r["bound"])
    worst_rel = max(worst["output"]["rel"], worst["state"]["rel"])
    ok = all(r["pass"] for r in rows)
    receipt = {"schema": PARITY_SCHEMA + "/recurrence", "tool": TOOL_NAME, "tool_version": TOOL_VERSION, "tool_sha256": file_sha256(__file__),
               "identity": identity_block(args, tree, engine), "needles": str(args.needles), "needles_sha256": manifest["needles_sha256"],
               "doc": doc["id"], "dtype": args.dtype, "device": device, "layers": chosen, "lengths": lengths, "chunks": chunk_sizes,
               "arms": arms, "reference": "tree KimiDeltaAttention.forward_with_state over the whole prefix (the stock streamed call)",
               "rows": rows, "worst": worst, "worst_rel": worst_rel, "threshold_rel": float(args.threshold_rel),
               "threshold_rel_kernel": float(args.threshold_rel_kernel), "triton_f32_default": os.environ.get("TRITON_F32_DEFAULT"),
               "verdict": "PASS" if ok else "FAIL", "seconds": round(time.monotonic() - started, 1), "memory": memory_block(device),
               "argv": sys.argv, "written_utc": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())}
    sha = write_json(args.out, receipt)
    by_arm = {}
    for r in rows:
        by_arm[r["arm"]] = max(by_arm.get(r["arm"], 0.0), r["output"]["rel"], r["state"]["rel"])
    print(f"RECURRENCE PARITY {'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'} ({device}, {args.dtype}, layers {chosen}, L {lengths}): worst rel "
          f"{worst_rel:.3e} ({worst['arm']}, layer {worst['layer']}, L={worst['length']}, chunk {worst['chunk']}) vs "
          f"{worst['bound']:.0e}; per arm " + ", ".join(f"{k} {v:.2e}" for k, v in by_arm.items())
          + f"; receipt {args.out} sha256 {sha[:16]}", flush=True)
    return 0 if ok else EXIT_REFUSED


def build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0], formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    parser.add_argument("--version", action="version", version=f"{TOOL_NAME} {TOOL_VERSION}")
    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)

    def common(p: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:
        p.add_argument("--review-tool", default=str(DEFAULT_REVIEW_TOOL))
        p.add_argument("--calibration-dir", default=os.environ.get("OC_CALIBRATION_DIR", str(DEFAULT_CALIBRATION)))

    p = sub.add_parser("build-needles", help="write the needle document set (safetensors + manifest)")
    common(p)
    p.add_argument("--tokenizer-dir", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--filler", default=str(OC / "distill/corpus/eval_split/eval_rows.jsonl"))
    p.add_argument("--lengths", default="4096,32768,131072,262144")
    p.add_argument("--depths", default="0.25,0.75")
    p.add_argument("--control-lengths", default="32768")
    p.add_argument("--seed", type=int, default=20261013)
    p.add_argument("--out", required=True)

    for name in ("parity", "read"):
        p = sub.add_parser(name)
        common(p)
        p.add_argument("--model", required=True)
        p.add_argument("--chimera-src", default=os.environ.get("CHIMERA_OMNI_TREE", str(DEFAULT_TREE)))
        p.add_argument("--needles", required=True)
        p.add_argument("--device", default="cuda:0")
        p.add_argument("--dtype", default="bfloat16", choices=("float32", "bfloat16", "float16"))
        p.add_argument("--kda-kernel", default="fla", choices=KDA_KERNELS)
        p.add_argument("--chunk", type=int, default=8192)
        p.add_argument("--attn-budget-mib", type=int, default=2048, help="fp32 score tensor budget per query sub-chunk")
        p.add_argument("--min-query-rows", type=int, default=16)
        p.add_argument("--no-band-mask", action="store_true", help="drop the ledger band logit mask (on by default, as in S8)")
        p.add_argument("--label", default="p11_omni1")
        p.add_argument("--parity-min-top1", type=float, default=0.95)
        p.add_argument("--parity-max-rel", type=float, default=1e-4, help="CPU fp32 arm: max |logit diff| / max |logit|")
        if name == "parity":
            p.add_argument("--length", type=int, default=4096)
            p.add_argument("--out", required=True)
        else:
            p.add_argument("--lengths", default="32768,131072,262144")
            p.add_argument("--parity-length", type=int, default=4096, help="run the parity arm at this length first (0 = skip)")
            p.add_argument("--out-dir", default=str(OC / "distill/tps"))

    p = sub.add_parser("rescore", help="1.1.0 readouts recovered from 1.0.0 read receipts (no model)")
    common(p)
    p.add_argument("--needles", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--receipts", required=True, help="comma-separated read receipts (p11_omni1_L*.json)")
    p.add_argument("--out", required=True)

    p = sub.add_parser("recurrence-parity", help="fp32 KDA recurrence: tree forward_with_state vs E2's loop / fla arms")
    common(p)
    p.add_argument("--model", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--chimera-src", default=os.environ.get("CHIMERA_OMNI_TREE", str(DEFAULT_TREE)))
    p.add_argument("--needles", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--device", default="cpu")
    p.add_argument("--dtype", default="float32", choices=("float32", "float64"))
    p.add_argument("--layers", default="auto", help="KDA block indices, or auto = the first three KDA blocks + the middle one")
    p.add_argument("--lengths", default="256,4096")
    p.add_argument("--chunks", default="96,1024", help="E2 chunk size per length for the chunked (state-carry) arm")
    p.add_argument("--arms", default="loop,fla-naive-recurrent,fla-naive-chunk", help="add fla on a CUDA device")
    p.add_argument("--threshold-rel", type=float, default=1e-4, help="bound for the torch reference arms (exact fp32 algebra)")
    p.add_argument("--threshold-rel-kernel", type=float, default=5e-3,
                   help="bound for the triton fla arm (its fp32 dots may be TF32; set TRITON_F32_DEFAULT=ieee to tighten)")
    p.add_argument("--out", required=True)
    return parser


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    args = build_parser().parse_args(argv)
    os.environ.setdefault("HF_HUB_OFFLINE", "1")
    os.environ.setdefault("TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE", "1")
    os.environ.setdefault("CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER", "PCI_BUS_ID")
    log(f"{TOOL_NAME} {TOOL_VERSION} {args.cmd}")
    try:
        if args.cmd == "build-needles":
            return cmd_build(args)
        if args.cmd == "parity":
            return cmd_parity(args)
        if args.cmd == "rescore":
            return cmd_rescore(args)
        if args.cmd == "recurrence-parity":
            return cmd_recurrence_parity(args)
        return cmd_read(args)
    except Refusal as exc:
        print(f"REFUSED: {exc}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        return EXIT_REFUSED


if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(main())
